## 1. MVVM Clean Architecture Diagrams

### Layered Architecture Flowchart

The diagram below illustrates how data and control flow between the **UI Layer (React Native)**, **ViewModel Layer (Custom Hooks)**, **Domain Layer (Pure TypeScript)**, and **Data Layer**.

```mermaid
graph TD
    subgraph UI_Layer ["1. UI Layer (Presentation)"]
        View["React Native Screen View (FC Component)"]
        State["UserProfileUiState (Discriminated Union)"]
        Styles["StyleSheet / Encapsulated Theme"]
    end

    subgraph ViewModel_Layer ["2. ViewModel / Controller Layer"]
        Hook["Custom ViewModel Hook (useUserProfileViewModel)"]
        Zustand["Zustand Store / TanStack Query"]
    end

    subgraph Domain_Layer ["3. Domain Layer (Pure Business Logic)"]
        UC["Use Cases (e.g. GetUserProfileUseCase)"]
        Model["Domain Models (Pure TypeScript Interfaces)"]
    end

    subgraph Data_Layer ["4. Data Layer (Single Source of Truth)"]
        Repo["UserRepositoryImpl"]
        Remote["Remote Axios / Fetch Client"]
        Local["Local Storage (MMKV / Keychain)"]
    end

    %% Flow interactions
    View -- "1. Invokes Handler Callback" --> Hook
    Hook -- "2. Dispatches State Transition" --> Zustand
    Hook -- "3. Executes Business Use Case" --> UC
    UC -- "4. Requests Repository Data" --> Repo
    Repo -- "5a. Fetches Remote API" --> Remote
    Repo -- "5b. Caches in MMKV / Keychain" --> Local
    Repo -- "6. Returns Domain Model" --> UC
    UC -- "7. Delivers Domain Result" --> Hook
    Hook -- "8. Updates State Hook" --> State
    State -- "9. Re-renders UI Screen" --> View

    %% Styling
    classDef uiStyle fill:#f2fbf5,stroke:#008544,stroke-width:2px;
    classDef vmStyle fill:#fefce8,stroke:#ca8a04,stroke-width:2px;
    classDef domainStyle fill:#eff6ff,stroke:#2563eb,stroke-width:2px;
    classDef dataStyle fill:#fef3c7,stroke:#d97706,stroke-width:2px;

    class View,State,Styles uiStyle;
    class Hook,Zustand vmStyle;
    class UC,Model domainStyle;
    class Repo,Remote,Local dataStyle;
```

